  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788608",
      "title": "Outputting User-specific Tasks",
      "lectureOrder": 46,
      "videoOrder": 42,
      "sourceHash": "a2a63db2a0bdef104398805f3d18bdaff7be5b288b0f52852d824cff326461de",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.33,
          "end": 3.15,
          "en": "So in order to now replace",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.15,
          "end": 5.43,
          "en": "this dummy fallback data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.43,
          "end": 8.07,
          "en": "with some more realistic data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.07,
          "end": 10.77,
          "en": "we can go to this tasks component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.77,
          "end": 12.75,
          "en": "which is responsible for outputting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.75,
          "end": 15.3,
          "en": "all those individual tasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.3,
          "end": 18.933,
          "en": "and simply add and manage a tasks array here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.19,
          "end": 22.59,
          "en": "So in the TasksComponent class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.59,
          "end": 26.58,
          "en": "we can add a new tasks property, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.58,
          "end": 29.1,
          "en": "Of course the name is up to you though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.1,
          "end": 32.13,
          "en": "And then set this equal to an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.13,
          "end": 36.72,
          "en": "where we could already add some dummy tasks if we wanted to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.72,
          "end": 39.76,
          "en": "for example, a task with an id of t1",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.71,
          "end": 45.39,
          "en": "with a title of Master Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.39,
          "end": 49.95,
          "en": "And then maybe a summary of \"Learn all the basic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.95,
          "end": 54.403,
          "en": "and advanced features of Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.403,
          "end": 57.18,
          "en": "& how to apply them.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.18,
          "end": 58.323,
          "en": "Anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.27,
          "end": 63.51,
          "en": "I also want to add a dueDate property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.51,
          "end": 66.99,
          "en": "to this task object so that we can output such a date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.99,
          "end": 68.7,
          "en": "for every task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.7,
          "end": 71.37,
          "en": "And that could be 2025",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.37,
          "end": 74.793,
          "en": "and then maybe December 31st,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.84,
          "end": 78.03,
          "en": "whatever, something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.03,
          "end": 82.2,
          "en": "Now every task should also be assigned to a user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.2,
          "end": 84.24,
          "en": "Therefore, every task object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.24,
          "end": 86.85300000000001,
          "en": "should also have a userId property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.84,
          "end": 91.47,
          "en": "which could be u1 for the first task",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.47,
          "end": 95.7,
          "en": "so that it's assigned to the user with the id u1,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.7,
          "end": 97.92,
          "en": "because we need to store this relation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.92,
          "end": 101.913,
          "en": "to make sure that different users have different tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.14,
          "end": 107.07,
          "en": "And of course we can now simply copy and paste that though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.07,
          "end": 108.47999999999999,
          "en": "to save you some time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.47999999999999,
          "end": 111.96000000000001,
          "en": "I prepared two additional dummy tasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.96000000000001,
          "end": 113.523,
          "en": "which you find attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.36,
          "end": 115.56,
          "en": "So that in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.56,
          "end": 117.9,
          "en": "your tasks array should look like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.9,
          "end": 120.453,
          "en": "with these three dummy tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.55,
          "end": 126.66,
          "en": "Well, and now that we do have those dummy tasks here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.66,
          "end": 128.07,
          "en": "we can and should of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.07,
          "end": 130.893,
          "en": "go to the tasks component template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.76,
          "end": 136.71,
          "en": "And instead of outputting those task components like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.71,
          "end": 141.363,
          "en": "we can now again output a dynamic list with @for,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.23,
          "end": 145.21,
          "en": "because now we can go through all those tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.16,
          "end": 150.85,
          "en": "and track the task ids to have some unique identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.89,
          "end": 155.67000000000002,
          "en": "and then output a list item with the app task inside of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.67000000000002,
          "end": 158.13,
          "en": "for every task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.13,
          "end": 161.79,
          "en": "Now with that, not much will change though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.79,
          "end": 165.42000000000002,
          "en": "We'll still output three tasks for every user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.42000000000002,
          "end": 167.79,
          "en": "no matter which user we select,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.79,
          "end": 170.34,
          "en": "because we're always outputting all the tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.34,
          "end": 171.69,
          "en": "for all the users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.69,
          "end": 173.82,
          "en": "And we have three tasks here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.82,
          "end": 177.32999999999998,
          "en": "So it's three tasks we're outputting for every user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.32999999999998,
          "end": 181.23,
          "en": "Now, of course, what we typically would want to do instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.23,
          "end": 184.29,
          "en": "is that we don't output all the tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.29,
          "end": 187.59,
          "en": "for all users, but instead only the tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.59,
          "end": 189.903,
          "en": "that belong to a certain user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 191.61,
          "end": 196.143,
          "en": "And we can achieve this by accepting another input here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.97,
          "end": 201.36,
          "en": "and that input would be the id",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 201.36,
          "end": 203.103,
          "en": "of the selected user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.57,
          "end": 208.11,
          "en": "And indeed, now we can actually also make this both required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.11,
          "end": 210.32999999999998,
          "en": "again, since we now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.32999999999998,
          "end": 213.15,
          "en": "due to the way the application works at this time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213.15,
          "end": 214.11,
          "en": "always know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 214.11,
          "end": 218.25,
          "en": "that we definitely should have an id and a name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 218.25,
          "end": 221.463,
          "en": "whenever this tasks component is being rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.41,
          "end": 226.95,
          "en": "But now that we also got this id of the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 226.95,
          "end": 231.36,
          "en": "for whom we're displaying this tasks component in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 231.36,
          "end": 234.813,
          "en": "we can also add another computed property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 235.71,
          "end": 237.06,
          "en": "another getter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 237.06,
          "end": 239.733,
          "en": "which could be called selectedUserTasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 242.46,
          "end": 246.31,
          "en": "where we return this.tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 247.35,
          "end": 250.41,
          "en": "and then we filter them for the tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 250.41,
          "end": 252.21,
          "en": "that belong to the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 252.21,
          "end": 255.45,
          "en": "And filter is another built in method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 255.45,
          "end": 257.493,
          "en": "built into JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 258.51,
          "end": 263.1,
          "en": "Like find, filter takes a function as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 263.1,
          "end": 266.1,
          "en": "And like the function you pass to find,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 266.1,
          "end": 270.51,
          "en": "this function you pass to filter will be executed once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 270.51,
          "end": 272.43,
          "en": "for every item in this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 272.43,
          "end": 274.65,
          "en": "and will then receive that item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 274.65,
          "end": 277.08,
          "en": "So that task in this case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 277.08,
          "end": 279.273,
          "en": "for which it is being executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 280.62,
          "end": 282.21,
          "en": "And we then have to return true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 282.21,
          "end": 285.39,
          "en": "if we want to keep the item in this filtered array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 285.39,
          "end": 287.493,
          "en": "or if we want to not have it there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 289.14,
          "end": 290.94,
          "en": "And here, my condition, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 290.94,
          "end": 295.94,
          "en": "is to check whether the userId is equal to this.id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 297.24,
          "end": 302.133,
          "en": "So to the userId we receive as an input here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 304.23,
          "end": 307.17,
          "en": "And of course we could name this userId here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 307.17,
          "end": 308.34,
          "en": "instead of just id",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 308.34,
          "end": 312.783,
          "en": "to make it really clear that this will be the id of a user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 315.39,
          "end": 318.57,
          "en": "With that change made, we have to go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 318.57,
          "end": 320.91,
          "en": "to the app component template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 320.91,
          "end": 323.613,
          "en": "where we're using our tasks here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 324.51,
          "end": 325.65,
          "en": "and we now also have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 325.65,
          "end": 329.02,
          "en": "to bind the userId property we just added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 330.24,
          "end": 335.24,
          "en": "and bind that to selectedUser.id in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 337.74,
          "end": 342.12,
          "en": "Now with that, we are able to filter out the tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 342.12,
          "end": 344.01,
          "en": "that belong to a user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 344.01,
          "end": 348.81,
          "en": "and we can now use this selectedUserTasks property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 348.81,
          "end": 349.92,
          "en": "in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 349.92,
          "end": 354.243,
          "en": "of this tasks component, in this loop here specifically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 355.14,
          "end": 359.49,
          "en": "So instead of going through all the tasks we possibly know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 359.49,
          "end": 362.49,
          "en": "we now want to go only through the tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 362.49,
          "end": 363.993,
          "en": "of the selected user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 366.21,
          "end": 370.08,
          "en": "And with those changes made, if you save all files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 370.08,
          "end": 373.08,
          "en": "you will see that different users now have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 373.08,
          "end": 375.81,
          "en": "different amounts of tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 375.81,
          "end": 378.6,
          "en": "We still don't output the task data here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 378.6,
          "end": 381.45,
          "en": "we still just got the dummy text here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 381.45,
          "end": 382.98,
          "en": "but that will change soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 382.98,
          "end": 387.45,
          "en": "But at least we are now outputting the tasks that do belong",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 387.45,
          "end": 388.863,
          "en": "to the different users.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
